Scanners

OpenQodex does not include any scanner. It downloads each scanner at run
time onto the user's machine, from the scanner's own release or package
registry. Each scanner keeps its own licence:

- semgrep, LGPL-2.1: https://github.com/semgrep/semgrep
- gitleaks, MIT: https://github.com/gitleaks/gitleaks
- bandit, Apache-2.0: https://github.com/PyCQA/bandit
- ruff, MIT: https://github.com/astral-sh/ruff
- oxlint, MIT: https://github.com/oxc-project/oxc
- osv-scanner, Apache-2.0: https://github.com/google/osv-scanner
- actionlint, MIT: https://github.com/rhysd/actionlint
- hadolint, GPL-3.0: https://github.com/hadolint/hadolint
- shellcheck, GPL-3.0: https://github.com/koalaman/shellcheck
- golangci-lint, GPL-3.0: https://github.com/golangci/golangci-lint
- brakeman, Brakeman Public Use License: https://github.com/presidentbeef/brakeman
  This is not an open source licence. OpenQodex does not bundle brakeman.
  It downloads brakeman at run time onto the user's machine.
- rubocop, MIT: https://github.com/rubocop/rubocop
- rubocop-rails, MIT: https://github.com/rubocop/rubocop-rails
- rubocop-performance, MIT: https://github.com/rubocop/rubocop-performance
- uv, Apache-2.0 or MIT: https://github.com/astral-sh/uv

Semgrep rules

semgrep fetches its rule packs from the Semgrep registry at run time, onto
the user's machine, for the user's own code. The rules are licensed under
the Semgrep Rules License v1.0: https://semgrep.dev/legal/rules-license
OpenQodex never bundles, vendors or redistributes them.

Code graph

The code graph parses source files with tree-sitter. The package ships the
tree-sitter runtime and six grammar files as WebAssembly in wasm/, unchanged
from the npm packages below. Each keeps its own licence:

- web-tree-sitter, MIT, Copyright (c) 2018 Max Brunsfeld:
  https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter
- @vscode/tree-sitter-wasm, MIT, Copyright (c) Microsoft Corporation:
  https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-tree-sitter-wasm
  It builds the grammar files from these grammars, each MIT licensed:
  - tree-sitter-typescript (typescript and tsx): https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-typescript
  - tree-sitter-javascript: https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-javascript
  - tree-sitter-python: https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-python
  - tree-sitter-go: https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-go
  - tree-sitter-ruby: https://github.com/tree-sitter/tree-sitter-ruby
